                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_496">Sheen, Surrey.
                        Charterhouse of Jesus of Bethlehem</orgName><p>Erased inscr. (10 lines) on
                        fol. ii verso (s. xv):</p><p>'[...] Iste liber pertinet [cancelled] [dom]us
                        Ihesu de bethleem</p><p>iuxta schen ordinis cart' [...] ad c[...] et
                        [...]ionem [?]</p><p>[...] et monachi sancti edmundi regis'</p><p>et
                        [martinis] [de bu]ry tempore [...] patre Iohanne Ing[il]b[y]</p><p>dicte
                        domus de Schen per me [...]</p><p>[...] dicta domo de Schen anno domini
                        1488o [?] quem ...</p><p>[...]ciis [?] remittere [...]etur [...] at [...]
                        </p><p>[...] se [...] poterit retinere aut alienare absque</p><p>consensu
                        Prioris dicte domus de Schen ‘tunc temporis’ existentis. S[i]</p><p>contra
                        fecerit s[it] anathema maranatha [?] Ihesus amen.'</p><p>John Ingilby was
                        prior 1479--1480.</p><p> At end, in red (s. xv): 'Liber Domus de Bethleem
                        ordinis Cartusien' de Schene. quem scripsit domnus Iohannes fferiby monachus
                        sacerdos et professus eiusdem domus ad honorem dei omnipotentis. sancte
                        marie uirginis. beati Nicholai confessoris sancte Katerine martiris. et
                        omnium sanctorum et in remissione peccatorum suorum. Amen.'</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Christopher Toottell (c. 1600).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'Ex dono Abelis de Sainte Marthe domini de
                     Corbenille in suprema vectigalium Curia senatoris', s. xvii ex.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'Datum huic Monasterio Sanctissimae
                     trinitatis Celestinorum de Marcoussiaco. 1691.'; all on fol. ii
                     verso.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">(fols. ii verso--iii recto) 'ad vsum Fratris
                     Laurentii Reyner Congreg. Anglicanae ordinis Sancti Benedicti', and 'Monasterii
                     D. Laurentii de Dei custodia', both in the same 17th-cent. hand.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Obtained by Rosenthal from
                     Portugal.</provenance>
               </history>
